## Known Limitations & Live Testing Notes

This resource's schema/model types are generated by `tfplugingen-framework`
from SailPoint's per-service `/source-apps/v1` OpenAPI spec, and
Create/Read/Update/Delete are hand-written against `golang-sdk/v3`'s
`apps.AppsAPIService` client.

- **`owner`, `access_profile_ids`, `enabled`, `provision_request_enabled`,
  and `app_center_enabled` are not accepted by the create API.** The API's
  `SourceAppCreateDto` only supports `name`, `description`, and
  `account_source` at create time. When any of the other attributes above
  are configured, the provider issues an immediate follow-up JSON Patch
  after the initial `POST` to set them - this means creating an application
  with those attributes configured always results in at least 2 API calls.
- **`access_profile_ids` is hand-added, not generated from the spec.**
  `GET /source-apps/v1/{id}` does not embed the application's access
  profiles, so the provider performs a separate, paginated
  `ListAccessProfilesForSourceApp` call on every `Read` to populate this
  attribute. Writes are sent via a JSON Patch `replace` on `/accessProfiles`
  with the full desired set of access profile ids (not incremental
  add/remove).
- **`owner` and `account_source` are converted by hand**, not via a
  generated `associated_external_type` helper, because the SDK's
  `BaseReferenceDto`/`SourceAppAccountSource` types don't map cleanly onto
  the generated nested object value types (`owner.type` in particular is a
  typed `DtoType` enum, not a plain string, in the SDK).
- **Updates are computed as a minimal JSON Patch diff** between plan and
  prior state (unlike some other resources in this provider that always send
  a full-document replace) - only attributes that actually changed are
  included in the `PATCH` request.
